module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Picard.HilbertFunctorFpqcGluing

/-!
# The sheaf property of the Hilbert functor, in the shape of its source

Let `X` be a scheme over `S` and let `d` be a natural number.
`Stacks.Hilbert.isSheaf_fpqcTopology_hilbertFunctorOfRank` says that the degree-`d` Hilbert
functor of points is a sheaf for the fpqc topology on the schemes over `S`, phrased for the
covering *sieves* of a Grothendieck topology. Stacks Tag 022G, which is the definition Tag 0B95
refers to, phrases the sheaf property for a covering *family*: for every fpqc covering
`{T i ⟶ T}` and every collection of elements `ξ i` agreeing on the fibre products
`T i ×_T T j`, there is a unique element over `T` restricting to each `ξ i`. This file records
the Hilbert functor's sheaf property in that shape.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Hilbert.existsUnique_hilbertFamily_of_mem_fpqcPrecoverage` — **Stacks Tag 0B95 in the
  shape of Stacks Tag 022G**: a collection of degree-`d` Hilbert families over the members of an
  fpqc covering family of `T` whose base changes to the pairwise fibre products agree is the
  collection of base changes of a unique degree-`d` Hilbert family over `T`.

## Implementation notes

Nothing here is new mathematics: the statement is deduced from
`Stacks.Hilbert.isSheaf_fpqcTopology_hilbertFunctorOfRank`. Its value is that the quantifiers,
the compatibility hypothesis and the uniqueness assertion are the source's, so the match with
the source can be read off rather than argued.

Three steps separate the two shapes. The fpqc topology on the schemes over `S` is generated by
the preimage of `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage` under `CategoryTheory.Over.forget`,
by `CategoryTheory.over_toGrothendieck_eq_toGrothendieck_comap_forget`; that preimage is stable
under base change and has pullbacks, so by
`CategoryTheory.Precoverage.isSheaf_toGrothendieck_iff_of_isStableUnderBaseChange` the sheaf
condition for the generated topology gives the sheaf condition for each covering family; and
`CategoryTheory.Presieve.isSheafFor_arrows_iff_pullbacks` converts the sheaf condition for a
family into the source's statement, replacing compatibility along arbitrary pairs of morphisms
with compatibility over the pairwise fibre products. The last step is the only one with
content, and it is an equivalence, so the statement below is neither weaker nor stronger than
the one it comes from.

The compatibility hypothesis and the fibre products are taken in `CategoryTheory.Over S`, which
is where the source takes them: the source's covering `{T i ⟶ T}` is a covering by `S`-schemes
and `T i ×_T T j` is their fibre product as `S`-schemes. Its underlying scheme is the fibre
product of the underlying schemes, so no information is lost.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B95](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B95)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 022G](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/022G)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry

universe u

namespace Stacks.Hilbert

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0B95, in the shape of the definition it refers to, Tag 022G.** Let
`X` be a scheme over `S`, let `d` be a natural number, and let `{g i : Y i ⟶ T}` be a family of
morphisms of `S`-schemes whose underlying family of morphisms of schemes is an fpqc covering of
`T`. Then a collection of degree-`d` Hilbert families `Z i` in `X` over `Y i` whose base changes
to the fibre products `Y i ×_T Y j` agree is the collection of base changes of a unique
degree-`d` Hilbert family in `X` over `T`. -/
@[stacks 0B95 "the sheaf property in the shape of Tag 022G: unique amalgamation for an \
arbitrary fpqc covering family, with compatibility over the pairwise fibre products"]
theorem existsUnique_hilbertFamily_of_mem_fpqcPrecoverage {S : Scheme.{u}} (X : Over S) (d : ℕ)
    {T : Over S} {ι : Type*} {Y : ι → Over S} (g : ∀ i, Y i ⟶ T)
    (hcov : Presieve.ofArrows (fun i ↦ (Y i).left) (fun i ↦ (g i).left) ∈
      Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage T.left)
    (Z : ∀ i, HilbertFamily X (Y i) d)
    (hZ : ∀ i j, baseChange X (pullback.fst (g i) (g j)) (Z i) =
      baseChange X (pullback.snd (g i) (g j)) (Z j)) :
    ∃! V : HilbertFamily X T d, ∀ i, baseChange X (g i) V = Z i := by
  have hmem : Presieve.ofArrows Y g ∈ Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage.comap (Over.forget S) T := by
    rw [Precoverage.mem_comap_iff, Presieve.map_ofArrows]
    exact hcov
  have hsheaf := isSheaf_fpqcTopology_hilbertFunctorOfRank X d
  rw [isSheaf_iff_isSheaf_of_type,
    CategoryTheory.over_toGrothendieck_eq_toGrothendieck_comap_forget Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage S,
    Precoverage.isSheaf_toGrothendieck_iff_of_isStableUnderBaseChange] at hsheaf
  exact (Presieve.isSheafFor_arrows_iff_pullbacks (P := hilbertFunctorOfRank X d)
    (X := Y) (π := g)).mp (hsheaf _ hmem) Z hZ

end Stacks.Hilbert

end
